  "notes": "University Park. Unlike the B.A. (six named options, PHILBA-2026.json), the B.S. has no options/concentrations -- one straightforward track, explicitly designed for double-majoring with STEM B.S. programs. Reuses phil_catalog.json entirely; every course in the four major-specific pools (Philosophical Foundations of Science: PHIL 11/13/110/125/126/126W/127/129; Ethics and Science: PHIL 107/118/132/133N/134; Advanced Topics: PHIL 403/407/410/425W/426W/427/432; plus PHIL 12 prescribed) was already cataloged from the B.A. build, all with no enforced prereqs. Real difference from the B.A.: no World Language sequence -- replaced by a 'Formal Reasoning' pool spanning CMPSC/ECON/IST/MATH/RM/SC/SRA/STAT, used twice (6cr). Real engine bug caught during verification: the bulletin's own Formal Reasoning list is almost entirely gated behind a MATH 110/140 prereq or concurrent that this plan never otherwise schedules (CMPSC 131 needs concurrent MATH 110/140, STAT 318 needs MATH 141, ECON 306 needs ECON 304) -- CMPSC 111 (a real but only 1-credit 'Logic for CS' course with no prereqs) was the sole exception, so reusing it for both Formal Reasoning slots caused the engine to reschedule the same 1cr course forever since a single already-completed course can't satisfy two separate plan items (see plan_progress's one-completed-course-per-item rule) and no second distinct option was ever eligible -- fixed by adding MATH 110 explicitly (Semester 1, satisfying GQ) so CMPSC 131 and STAT 184 both become genuinely eligible, giving the Formal Reasoning pool two real distinct completable options. The bulletin's own 'Supporting Courses' unrestricted PHIL elective is modeled as a literal PHIL 1 pick.",
